# Swift macOS Architecture

Prefer SwiftUI. Reach for AppKit only behind a thin wrapper when SwiftUI cannot do it.

## File & module shape

- One primary type per file. Split a file when it exceeds ~150 lines or mixes concerns.
- Group by feature, not by layer dumping ground:

```
AirScript/
  App/                 # AirScriptApp, scene, app state
  DesignSystem/        # tokens, materials, shared chrome
  Features/<Name>/     # Views, ViewModels, feature models
  Models/              # SwiftData / domain types
  Services/            # I/O, persistence, system APIs
  Shared/              # cross-feature components & extensions
```

- Views compose; they do not own networking, disk, or business rules.
- Extract a subview, `ViewModifier`, or component the second a block is reused or nested >2 levels.
- Keep `ContentView` as a shell (tabs/split/navigation). Put screens in feature folders.

## Abstraction & reuse

- Depend on protocols at feature boundaries (`ScriptRunning`, `SettingsStoring`). Inject via init or `@Environment`.
- Use `@Observable` (or a focused `@Observable` type) for view models — not god objects.
- SwiftData `@Model` types stay in `Models/`. Views talk to them through queries or a store, not ad-hoc `modelContext` sprinkled everywhere.
- Shared chrome lives in `DesignSystem/` (glass panels, toolbars, list rows). Feature views must not duplicate materials, radii, or spacing literals.
- Prefer small pure functions and value types. Classes/`@Model` only for identity or persistence.

## Native macOS UI structure

- Use `WindowGroup`, `Settings`, `MenuBarExtra`, `NavigationSplitView`, `Inspector`, and `commands` instead of custom window chrome.
- Toolbar actions go in `.toolbar`; do not fake a macOS toolbar with `HStack`.
- Every public `View` gets a `#Preview` with realistic data (in-memory store when SwiftData is involved).

```swift
// ❌ BAD — logic, layout, and persistence in one file
struct ContentView: View {
    var body: some View {
        VStack { /* 200 lines of cards, queries, and mutations */ }
    }
}

// ✅ GOOD — shell + feature view + injected store
struct ContentView: View {
    var body: some View {
        NavigationSplitView {
            ScriptListView()
        } detail: {
            ScriptEditorView()
        }
    }
}
```

- Access control: `private` unless another file needs it. No `public` unless it is a module boundary.
- Name types by role (`GlassPanel`, `ScriptListView`, `ScriptStore`), not `Manager`/`Helper`/`Utils`.
